 of the agent file as the sub-agent's prompt. The planner file has `model: opus` in its frontmatter, but the MODEL RULE says absolutely never to specify a model in the spawn call. subagent_type also shouldn't be set unless instructed. Per the contract: \"Do not set `subagent_type` / `run_in_background` / `name` unless instructed below.\" So spawn the default workflow subagent with prompt = entire content of agent file + task.\n\nNote: the planner agent's frontmatter specifies model opus and tools Read/Grep/Glob (read-only). Since I'm passing the content as a prompt to the default subagent, the subagent will follow those instructions. The planner is a read-only role — no problem.\n\nThe implementation agent needs tools (Write, Bash) — the default `claude` agent type has all tools. Per the contract, don't set subagent_type. OK.\n\nSo let me spin up the planner agent in the background (default). Then wait via TaskOutput.\n\nActually, I'll run in the background by default and be notified. So spin up the planner, then wait via TaskOutput block. Let me compose the prompt.\n\nPlanner prompt = full content of ecc-planner.md + task:\n\nTask description for the planner:\n- Story STORY-setup-001a: create the root package.json for the NextMove monorepo.\n- Workspace root path, branch iotahub/phase-1, existing git repo (do not reinitialize).\n- Node v22.23.2, npm 10.9.8 already installed.\n- requirements...\n- Deliverable: markdown plan including implementation steps, test strategy (sample unit test mapping 1:1 to AC using node:test), risks, success criteria.\n\nNote: the planner agent's toolset is Read/Grep/Glob (read-only) — the planner should not write files, just output the plan. That's fine — the plan will be returned as text.\n\nThen the implementation sub-agent receives planner's plan + task.\n\nAlso, the implementation sub-agent \"must load `tdd-workflow` before coding\" — instruct it to read .claude/skills/tdd-workflow/SKILL.md. Let me check whether that skill file exis